<!--Post: 4117--><!--Time: 1105697184-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4117"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 2:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know if there were a series of sheep or horse killings between 1955-1974 in Witchata. Were there any arrests or any suspects? I&#39;m sure he started out that way. By torturing and killing animals. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4117-->
<!--Post: 4135--><!--Time: 1105737987-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4135"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 1:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would probably require an archive search through local newspaper and police files, in other words...I have no idea.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4135-->
<!--Post: 4139--><!--Time: 1105740252-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4139"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 2:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe there is a high correlation between killers and hunters.  <BR> <BR>Often I see in the paper where the neighbors knew the killer was violent as a child. In one article I read something like “he stabbed a dog in the neighborhood.”  <BR> <BR>In another article there was a picture of a kid who had killed his father – he was holding his hunting prize -- a deer head.  <BR> <BR>If you think about it, who would actually GET ENJOYMENT out of stalking &amp; killing a deer and watching it suffer and die &#40;possibly with little offspring looking on&#41;?  <BR> <BR>It is cruel, and personally I don’t think it is a sport.  <BR> <BR>Anyway, I believe you are correct Nugzter, BTK probably had some kind of tendancies that might lead him to torture helpless animals.  <BR> <BR>I wonder if the area Humane Society has any records of prosecuting people in the area around that time? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4139-->
<!--Post: 4162--><!--Time: 1105801109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4162"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ah, the deadly triad. bed-wetting past age 12, arson, and animal cruelty/torture. i&#39;m sure it has all been considered.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4162-->
<!--Post: 4163--><!--Time: 1105802027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4163"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 7:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iceteajan, let me start out by saying that I am in no way a hunter. If I were to go out in the woods, I would get lost, LOL! To think about taking aim at an animal, it gets me queasy. People very close to me are hunters, and with what I know about them, there is no similarity between BTK and them. They view stalking and killing their game more humane than what we do to our beef stock. When they do get a kill, they don&#39;t have just a dead animal, they have meat for months, and there is a lot you can do with the rest of the animal. Hunters don&#39;t go out and kill any animal and just take their heads. They have respect for the animal, and not to mention that the animal gets away more than they are hunted. It&#39;s not a sport, I agree with you on that. <BR> <BR>I think that there is a much higher correlation between killers and animal abusers. Like the first comparison that you made with the kid that stabbed a dog in the neighborhood. Dog and cat abusers/killers seem to be a gateway to crimes against people. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4163-->
<!--Post: 4204--><!--Time: 1105850362-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 8:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A better correlation for serial killers is ..for males..children who wet the bed..become pyromaniacs..that is start fires..or who kill/trap/torture small animals....small animals not large ones like horses...Dahmer killed small animals....The problem would be getting access to state mental health records..if BTK was ever treated for bedwetting..or possibly killing animals such as the neighbors pets...or was ever charged with or accused of doing such things as a juvenile...such court records and/or police records are often sealed if the crime is commited by a juvenile...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4204-->
<!--Post: 4247--><!--Time: 1105963588-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4247"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 4:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->True Angry, but what about when he was older. Some serial killers kill horses as a test of their power and control. 16-30 is the age group for horse killings.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4247-->
<!--Post: 4290--><!--Time: 1106047109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4290"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 18, 2005 - 3:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The reason I came to the horse killings is I saw an interview with an Austrian serial killer and he would stab a horse to death then slit it open and take his clothes off and actaull get inside the carcas and try to have sex with the guts. Now this guy was only maybe 5ft7in. Thats a hell of a task, but he did it. And uppon reasearch the police had the horse killings on record years before the guy started killing people. He compared it to graduating into the big leagues.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
